{"term":"germinate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a1f63f8b88db969077","definition":"Of a seed, to begin to grow, to sprout roots and leaves.","example":"the Chalcites, which hath a Spirit that will put forth and germinate","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ackerspyre"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["autogerminate","degerminator","germinative","ingerminate","nongerminated","pregerminated","regerminate","ungerminated","ungerminating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/germinate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6589312a7e696e2c7f","definition":"To cause to grow; to produce.","example":"These were business hours, and a feeling of loneliness crept over him, perhaps germinated by his sight of the illustrated papers, and accentuated by an attempted perusal of them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ackerspyre"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["autogerminate","degerminator","germinative","ingerminate","nongerminated","pregerminated","regerminate","ungerminated","ungerminating"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/germinate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈd͡ʒɜː(ɹ)mɪneɪt/"},"wordFamily":["autogerminate","degerminator","germinative","ingerminate","nongerminated","pregerminated","regerminate","ungerminated","ungerminating"]}